# Depth Perspectives
#
# Two versions of the same paragraph, and a way to move between them. The design
# has been wanted for a while and stalls in the same place every time: the
# versions do not carry the same information, and "simple" is not one thing.
# This names why, and what would have to be true for arrows to work.

#>depth_perspectives
#:convention #!copy #!pedagogy #!perspective
#:operation #!prime
#:fixity #!experimental
#:layer #!pragmatics

@expressive_registers: ~"./expressive-registers.spw"
@semantic_expression: ~"./semantic-expression-consequence.spw"
@arrival_electrostatics: ~"./arrival-electrostatics.spw"
@copy_localization: ~"./copy-localization.spw"
@attribute_governance: ~"./data-spw-attribute-governance.spw"
@copy_lens_css: ~"../../public/css/systems/semantic-copy-lens.css"
@familiarity_gate: ~"../../public/js/runtime/familiarity-gate.js"
@precipitates: ~"../_workbench/.spw/runtime/precipitates.spw"

operation = "prime"
fixity = "experimental"

expression = topic[perspective]{holds.drops.assumes}<traverse>

^"the_stall"{
  claim: "Left and right arrows imply a total order. The versions do not have one, so the control promises something the content cannot deliver."
  not_conserved: "A beginner version is not a subset of an advanced one. It carries analogy, motivation and scaffolding the advanced version drops, and drops precision, edge cases and formalism the advanced version needs. Neither contains the other."
  simple_is_not_one_thing: "Fewer concepts, more concrete, shorter, less jargon, more motivated — these are different requests that all arrive under the word simple, and they pull apart. A version that is shorter is often less concrete, because concreteness costs words."
  consequence: "Ranking versions 1..N forces a single axis onto a set that has several, and the ranking is where the disagreement about what simple means gets buried instead of expressed."
}

^"measured_conflation"{
  claim: "The attribute that would carry this already mixes two axes."
  attribute = `data-spw-copy-depth`
  values_in_use: .{
    normal = 91
    genre = 11
    rich = 5
    entry = 5
    technical = 2
  }[reg=facet]
  problem: "entry | normal | rich is a depth ladder. genre | technical is a register. They are orthogonal — technical-entry and genre-rich are both coherent and neither is expressible."
  probe: `grep -rho 'data-spw-copy-depth="[^"]*"' --include=index.html . | sed 's/.*="\(.*\)"/\1/' | sort | uniq -c`
  status: "Nothing selects between versions today. 114 declarations, all consumed by CSS for styling; no route authors two versions of the same paragraph."
}

^"three_axes_that_get_confused"{
  ~#note: "Keeping these apart is most of the design."
  text_depth: "A property of the writing. How much is unpacked. Authored."
  text_register: "A property of the writing. Which vocabulary it reaches for — genre, technical, plain. Authored, and independent of depth."
  reader_familiarity: "A property of the reader, measured — fresh | familiar | practiced | fluent | habitual per @familiarity_gate. Not a property of any version."
  rule: "Do not let measured familiarity choose the version silently. A fluent reader often wants the beginner version — to teach from, to check an intuition, to remember how it felt. Familiarity may suggest a default; only the reader may set it."
}

^"projection_not_rank"{
  claim: "Versions are projections of one concept through different lenses, not rungs on a ladder. @precipitates already defines projection as 'a view of one stage's output through another stage's lens' — the lenses are not ranked there either."
  consequence: "If each version declares what it holds and what it drops, difference becomes inspectable instead of implied. `holds` and `drops` are the interesting fields; `depth` was never the interesting field."
  shape: `topic[perspective]{holds.drops.assumes}`
  kinship: "Two versions share a subject and differ in mode, which makes them kin by subject under @semantic_expression — the conceptual space asked for is the kinship graph that already exists."
  traversal: "Arrows still work. They traverse a graph rather than a line, and the control has to say which edge it is following — 'more concrete' is a different arrow from 'more precise'."
}

^"what_would_make_it_buildable"{
  ~#note: "Not built. This is a prime — the path, not the patch."
  first: "Split the conflated attribute. Depth and register need separate stems before anything can select on either."
  second: "Author one concept twice, in one place, with holds/drops declared. One worked example teaches more than a schema."
  third: "Measure conservation across the pair — what does each carry that the other does not. If the answer is 'the same content, fewer words', the versions are not perspectives and the feature is not needed."
  fourth: "Only then a control, and it names its edge rather than a direction."
  refuse: "Do not ship arrows over versions that were written as a ladder. The control would be honest and the content would not."
}

#>wonder_depth_perspectives_1
?["Is there a version of a paragraph that every other version can be derived from?"]{
  #:depth #!educational ~#lens(conservation)
  ~#tension: "authoring N versions by hand is N times the maintenance and they drift. deriving them from one source assumes a source that contains everything, and the beginner version's analogy is not in the technical one — it was invented for the reader, not extracted from the concept."
  ~#hypothesis: "no. the union of all versions is larger than any of them, so the source would have to be a structure rather than a text — closer to holds/drops than to prose."
  !probe{ "take one concept, write it for a newcomer and for someone fluent, then list what each carries that the other does not. if either list is empty the versions are a ladder; if both are full they are perspectives and no single source generates them." }
  $%[version.holds, version.drops, version.assumes, concept.subject]
}

#>wonder_depth_perspectives_2
?["Whose simple is the default?"]{
  #:depth #!experiential ~#lens(register)
  ~#tension: "the site's audience now includes mentees being onboarded, a token community, and a table of players — three groups whose simple is different. a single default picks one of them and calls it neutral."
  ~#hypothesis: "the default belongs to the route rather than the site. a recipe page's simple is concrete; an operator atlas's simple is fewer concepts; they should not share a setting."
  !probe{ "for three routes with different audiences, write the same sentence at each one's simple. if the three differ in kind rather than in length, the default is route-scoped." }
  $%[route.audience, version.register, version.holds]
}

^"validation"{
  probe: `grep -rho 'data-spw-copy-depth="[^"]*"' --include=index.html . | sort | uniq -c`
  falsification: #[
    `Two versions of one concept ship with a depth rank and no holds/drops declaration.`,
    `Measured familiarity selects a version without the reader choosing it.`,
    `A control offers direction (more/less) rather than an edge (more concrete / more precise).`
  ][reg=set]
  next: "One concept, authored twice, with holds and drops written down. Everything else waits on that."
}
